    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Render Your Cards\r\n\r\nYour dataset has some missing values. Your job is to work with AI Tutor to build your card from your Level 3 design, then write the conditional checks that handle missing data — so every card displays cleanly, no matter what's null.\r\n\r\n::: details [1. **Observe the cards that have been started for you:**]\r\nYou should see image-only cards on the screen - one for each movie in the dataset.\r\n:::\r\n::: details [2. **Upload your card view from your Backpack:**] \r\nShare it with AI Tutor and prompt AI Tutor to update the cards to match your design.\r\n:::\r\n::: details [3. **Evaluate AI's output:**] \r\nDo the cards match your design from Level 3? If not, deteremine what needs to change and prompt AI again. Once it looks right, accept the changes.\r\n:::\r\n::: details [4. **Write your fallback checks in `script.js`:**] \r\nThe loop is already set up. Inside the fallback section, work with AI to write conditional checks for each field that might be null. Use the fallback values you planned in Level 3.\r\n:::\r\n::: details [5. **Test your cards:**] \r\nRun the code and check every card. Each one should display cleanly — no blank spaces, no broken images, no missing text.\r\n:::",
